/*
 * Declares the TraitRefType class.
 *
 * A TraitRefType is a temporary placeholder used during semantic validation to
 * refer to a trait symbol. It does not represent a concrete runtime type and is
 * never emitted into YIL. Its purpose is simply to carry a reference to a
 * TraitSymbol from the symbol table until the trait is resolved or used in
 * validation(e.g., checking trait implementations).
 *
 * This type appears during intermediate stages of validation when a trait is
 * known syntactically but its instantiation or usage context is not yet fully
 * determined.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::type::temporary::traitref
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/type/temporary/traitref.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-26
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
